From: OfficeDroid contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: read private Android PE images into anonymous memory

Modern Android denies executable mappings of app-data files. Initial RW file
mapping can succeed, leaving the later RX protection change to fail. Select
Wine's existing read fallback before mapping the PE header and private sections.
The explicit shared-section mapping paths remain unchanged.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the modified Wine file.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3037,6 +3037,12 @@
 
     TRACE_(module)( "mapping PE file %s at %p-%p\n", debugstr_us(nt_name), ptr, ptr + total_size );
 
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    /* App-data files cannot acquire PROT_EXEC. Copy private image pages into
+     * the anonymous view; Wine applies each section's final protections below. */
+    removable = TRUE;
+#endif
+
     /* map the header */
 
     fstat( fd, &st );
